    "content": "The Artemis II crew consists of four astronauts scheduled for a 10-day mission around the Moon in 2026: NASA Commander Reid Wiseman, Pilot Victor Glover, Mission Specialist Christina Koch, and Canadian Space Agency (CSA) Mission Specialist Jeremy Hansen. They are the first crewed flight to orbit the Moon since Apollo 17. This video introduces the Artemis II crew members:28sFOX54 News HuntsvilleYouTube• Mar 31, 2026 28s Reid Wiseman (Commander): A U.S. Navy pilot and former chief of the astronaut office, this is his second spaceflight. Victor Glover (Pilot): A U.S. Navy captain who piloted the SpaceX Crew-1 mission, he will be the first Black astronaut to fly around the Moon. Christina Koch (Mission Specialist): Holds the record for the longest single spaceflight by a woman and participated in the first all-woman spacewalk. Jeremy Hansen (Mission Specialist): A Canadian Space Agency astronaut making his first spaceflight, he serves as Canada's first astronaut for a lunar mission. This mission tests the Orion spacecraft systems before future lunar landing missions.",
